A||||4||Phoenix||88 lower ball joints||||1||
Z||000000||Phoenix||06-02-2000||11:59 PM||||Anyone replaced the lower ball joints on an 88 themselves? Did you do it with the a-arms on the car or is it easier to do it with them off? How large of a press is needed to get them out? Any suggestions/help greatly appreciated.<P>TIA||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phaeton||06-03-2000||02:37 AM||||My Fiero has been way too good to me.  Hasn't actually broken anything in years and years.<P>The A arm did not have to come off, that I'm sure of.<BR>I seem to remember putting a jackstand under the arm to support it and taking an air chisel to some rivet heads.<P>Or was that my Olds?  Hah, they're both GM products so it shouldn't make any difference.  Aren't they all the same?<P>I rode in a diesel chevette once (just so you know I'm kidding).<P>After the rivet heads are off the rivets still have to be punched out, they in there tight.  That jackstand or equivalent is necessary to keep the arm solid, other wise it flops something fierce and won't take a solid enough hit.<P>Don't recall needing a press.  Not sure if I needed my 'won't go' hammer or not thoough.||||reg||12
Z||000002||Phoenix||06-03-2000||10:00 AM||||Ok - Thanks, that sound correct for the upper ball joints, the lower ones are pressed in on the 88's and those are the ones I need to replace ||||reg||7
Z||000003||Phaeton||06-03-2000||12:05 PM||||Uh oh.<BR>Was it the Fiero's that I took the A arm off, torched it cherry, pounded the stud out the bottom with the 'won't go', chiseled the shell out of the socket, then ground off all protrusions so the new ball joint would go in?  And the wussies at the alignment shop refused to touch it, insisted on a whole new A arm.<BR>No wait, that was a Pinto.  I'm gonna have to pull the tire and look, maybe that will jog a memory or two.<P>I can't remember when it left, but its gone.  Just wait, all you young suckers, it'll happen to you too.  Folks will look at you funny and ask "what the he11 is a whippersnapper?" and you'll have forgotten that also. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000004||Phoenix||06-03-2000||01:01 PM||||Well - Well,  I don't know how old you are but I'm a product of growing up in the early 60's so we probable can relate to things.  I've got the a-arms off and I'm going to press them them out.  a B.F.H. and a tourch would probably work also but there is the issue of the alignment shop working on it.  I'm going to have a beer and kick back now have a good weekend. ||||reg||12
